Laya (English checkpoint), ONNX 8-bit build for app-cargo-laya
===============================================================

This directory contains a modified version of the Laya decision model:

  Laya by Convai Innovations
  https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE)

Laya's backbone is ModernBERT-large by Answer.AI and LightOn
(https://huggingface.co/answerdotai/ModernBERT-large), also licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. The tokenizer (tokenizer/tokenizer.json) and
rl_agent_config.json are copied unchanged from convaiinnovations/laya.

Changes made for Acurast, 2026-09-24, to model.safetensors:
  - exported the encoder and the decision head to one ONNX graph
    (laya.onnx + laya.onnx.data) with torch.onnx (dynamo exporter, opset 18)
  - quantized the MatMul weights to 8 bits (ONNX Runtime MatMulNBits,
    block size 32, symmetric, accuracy level 4)
The answers differ slightly from the original (probabilities within 0.05 on
our checks). The export script is tools/export_model.py in
https://github.com/Acurast/acurast-example-apps (apps/app-cargo-laya).

This build is not endorsed by Convai Innovations, Answer.AI or LightOn.
